1
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:30,380
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Supervised agencies, colleagues in the Senate, Senator Aimee, magandang hapon po sa ating lahat.

2
00:10:31,120 --> 00:11:07,500
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Today we will hear the proposed Fiscal Year 2027 budget of the Department of Social Welfare and Development. Sa budget hearing na ito, simple ang prinsipyo natin. Kapag may pamilyang nagugutom, nawawala ng trabaho o kabuhayan, nakakasakit o tinatamaan ng sakuna, dapat may gobyernong sasalo. I’m fully aware that the House-approved GAAB provides P262.757 billion in new appropriations for DSWD, higher than the NEP, although still below the 2026 GAA program level.

3
00:11:07,500 --> 00:11:31,440
Senator Risa Hontiveros: We take note of the adjustments made by our colleagues in the House of Representatives. AICS increases to about 58.1 billion pesos. The Quick Response Fund is restored to 3 billion pesos. The Sustainable Livelihood Program increases to almost 6 billion pesos. But more money must mean better social protection.

4
00:11:31,440 --> 00:11:56,060
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Una, we must protect 4Ps as a rights-based investment in poor families and their children. If families graduate from 4Ps, graduation must mean more than losing a grant. They should have a real pathway to education, skills, employment, livelihood, and continued access to basic services. Hindi graduation ang mawalan ng benepisyo.

5
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:59,940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pangalawa, we must protect our senior citizens.

6
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:11,520
Senator Risa Hontiveros: The social pension remains a lifeline for millions of indigent seniors, yet many qualified senior citizens remain on the waiting or remain waiting for assistance.

7
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:21,800
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At 1,000 pesos a month, we must also keep asking whether the benefit remains adequate given the rising cost of food, medicine, and transportation.

8
00:12:22,700 --> 00:12:27,680
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pangatlo, AICs must remain a genuine social safety net.

9
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:30,240
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ang tulong ay hindi pabor.

10
00:12:31,040 --> 00:12:37,220
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Dapat nakabatay sa pangangailangan, hindi sa kung sino ang kakilala o kung sino ang nag-refer.

11
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:52,940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: We need stronger controls against duplicate payments, but digitization must not exclude people without bank accounts, without a phone, with poor connectivity, or with incomplete records.

12
00:12:53,420 --> 00:12:57,660
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Pang-apat, we must also prepare for the Super El Niño and other climate shocks.

13
00:12:57,680 --> 00:13:15,340
Senator Risa Hontiveros: The restoration of the QRF is important, but DSWD must be ready before families reach a crisis point with food assistance, emergency cash, cash for work, livelihood support, and coordination with LGUs.

14
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:26,160
Senator Risa Hontiveros: At the same time, we recognize DSWD's investment in disaster response and rehabilitation programs, such as Project Lawa at Binhi,

15
00:13:26,160 --> 00:13:35,120
Senator Risa Hontiveros: as well as its investment in longer-term climate resilience through the Philippine Community Resilience Project or Panahon ng Pagkilos.

16
00:13:35,780 --> 00:13:40,100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Emergency response and long-term resilience must work together,

17
00:13:40,620 --> 00:13:46,460
Senator Risa Hontiveros: helping communities survive today's shocks while reducing their vulnerability to future disasters.

18
00:13:47,160 --> 00:13:51,940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: We also welcome the allocation of resources to support vulnerable groups

19
00:13:51,940 --> 00:13:57,040
Senator Risa Hontiveros: through Enhanced Protect Teen, Project Aruga, Project SAFE,

20
00:13:57,680 --> 00:14:01,140
Senator Risa Hontiveros: and the Special Committee on LGBTQIA Plus Affairs,

21
00:14:01,720 --> 00:14:06,540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: programs and initiatives that support adolescent mothers and their families,

22
00:14:07,160 --> 00:14:09,300
Senator Risa Hontiveros: children with disabilities and their caregivers,

23
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:13,540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: child survivors of online sexual abuse and exploitation,

24
00:14:14,340 --> 00:14:17,260
