DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: with focus on poor and near-poor families.

559
00:35:25,060 --> 00:35:30,800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Beyond budget utilization, we measure 4Ps by its results and ensure that our programs are guided by evidence.

560
00:35:30,800 --> 00:35:49,720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: From 2022 to July 2026, 1.77 million households graduated to self-sufficiency, 7.24 million children completed primary and secondary education, and 78,886 beneficiaries passed licensure examinations,

561
00:35:49,740 --> 00:35:52,760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: including 259 top-notchers.

562
00:35:53,280 --> 00:36:03,000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Under the F1KD First 1,000 Days grant, 83.9% of pregnant beneficiaries nationwide completed the required prenatal visits.

563
00:36:03,740 --> 00:36:06,680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These results are reinforced by independent studies.

564
00:36:06,940 --> 00:36:17,600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The World Bank's 2026 study attributed a 2.2% point reduction in national poverty to 4Ps and estimated a 4.4 cost-benefit ratio.

565
00:36:17,600 --> 00:36:21,600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: The Brain Trust Study also recognizes the program's educational impact.

566
00:36:22,300 --> 00:36:23,700
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: in its reach among poor households.

567
00:36:24,380 --> 00:36:35,560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These findings strengthen our commitment to evidence-informed policymaking, continuous program improvement, and ensuring that the public resources deliver measurable results for Filipino families.

568
00:36:36,220 --> 00:36:44,800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Under protective services, AICS remains our primary program for individuals and families in crisis, complemented by community-based services for vulnerable sectors.

569
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:50,300
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In 2025, we utilize 100% of the budget, assisting over 9.4 million beneficiaries.

570
00:36:51,040 --> 00:36:51,980
