DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Meaning, lesser sub-projects, itong mga pre-identified na targets, hindi hun lahat mabibigyan.

4318
02:59:33,360 --> 02:59:38,000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, the worry there is also, I don't think the development agency will like that

4319
02:59:38,000 --> 02:59:44,580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: because when we did sign the commitment, meron na yung pre-identified mechanisms and the designs are already preset.

4320
02:59:45,680 --> 02:59:46,560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ongoing na ito?

4321
02:59:46,900 --> 02:59:49,940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ongoing na po. In fact, we're doing the first round this year.

4322
02:59:50,220 --> 02:59:50,520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

4323
02:59:50,520 --> 02:59:52,340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: It's a five-year plan.

4324
02:59:53,260 --> 02:59:54,880
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Until 2031.

4325
02:59:55,340 --> 02:59:58,260
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay. And then, ang counterpart natin is 10 billion.

4326
02:59:59,200 --> 02:59:59,780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Is correct.

4327
02:59:59,980 --> 03:00:00,620
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: 10 billion.

4328
03:00:02,120 --> 03:00:08,520
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Dito sa original na P17 billion, nandito na yung counterpart.

4329
03:00:15,020 --> 03:00:20,460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nandito na yung counterpart pero ang nabawasan po ay yung ODA side.

4330
03:00:20,680 --> 03:00:21,840
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Ah, yung ODA side.

4331
03:00:21,860 --> 03:00:22,980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: At the COP side.

4332
03:00:23,580 --> 03:00:23,920
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

4333
03:00:23,920 --> 03:00:24,060
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

4334
03:00:24,060 --> 03:00:35,860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay. Will it help? Ang mangyayari dito dahil nabawasan ng P5.4, beneficiary?

4335
03:00:35,980 --> 03:00:39,980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Liliit. Yes. And when we talk about beneficiaries, communities. LGUs.

4336
03:00:40,120 --> 03:00:46,960
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: And how many communities ang mababawasan with that P5.5 cut?

4337
03:00:54,060 --> 03:01:02,100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Madam Chair, hindi ho mababawasan yung physical target pero ang liliit ho yung matatanggap nila na grant.

4338
03:01:02,500 --> 03:01:05,560
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So we'll have to proportionally apply the cut everywhere.

4339
03:01:06,080 --> 03:01:12,340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So halimbawa, ang na-initial na, kasi the whole concept there is they are pre-identified using the filters.

4340
03:01:12,720 --> 03:01:19,020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Meron ba diya ang mataas bang poverty incidents, stunting incident, meron bang presence ng indigenous people,

4341
03:01:19,020 --> 03:01:22,000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and susceptible ba kayo sa climate change or disasters.

4342
03:01:22,660 --> 03:01:24,020
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So nung na-identify na sila,

4343
03:01:24,460 --> 03:01:27,960
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: we gathered the LGUs already and notified them of their allocations

4344
03:01:27,960 --> 03:01:29,900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: and beneficiary na sila.

4345
03:01:30,300 --> 03:01:32,240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So they made their community planning already.

4346
03:01:32,860 --> 03:01:35,180
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Now, babalikan namin sila at sasabihin namin sa kanila,

4347
03:01:35,280 --> 03:01:38,760
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: yung plinano nyo, if that was no more than 20 million, liliit ho yun.

4348
03:01:39,380 --> 03:01:40,520
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So they'll have to scale down.

4349
03:01:40,600 --> 03:01:43,120
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Pagkano makukuha nila? Originally it was 20 million.

4350
03:01:43,340 --> 03:01:44,660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: No more than 20 million yan.

4351
03:01:44,980 --> 03:01:46,460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For sub-projects.

4352
03:01:46,940 --> 03:01:47,380
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yeah.

4353
03:01:48,520 --> 03:01:51,360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: For every year kasi no more than 20 million ho yan.

4354
03:01:51,440 --> 03:01:52,540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: These are micro-projects.

4355
03:01:52,600 --> 03:01:53,460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We're talking about pathways.

4356
03:01:54,060 --> 03:01:57,640
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We're talking about pathways, bridges, yung pinakita ko kanina, yung water system.

4357
03:01:58,160 --> 03:02:02,240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So that's 20 to 20 million for the span of 3 years.

4358
03:02:02,360 --> 03:02:07,060
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So mga 50 to 70 million for the span of 5 years.

4359
03:02:07,500 --> 03:02:08,680
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: 3 years, sorry, 3 years.

4360
03:02:08,820 --> 03:02:10,000
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So yun ang mababawasan ho.

4361
03:02:10,520 --> 03:02:11,980
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Proportionately, we'll have to cut it.

4362
03:02:12,180 --> 03:02:14,080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Baka wala na silang matapos with that.

4363
03:02:14,440 --> 03:02:18,560
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Siyempre, the smaller the project, the less the impact, di ba?

4364
03:02:18,700 --> 03:02:19,780
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Madam Chair, that's the fear.

4365
03:02:19,780 --> 03:02:24,040
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And more so, maliliit na nga siya kasi they're micro-infrastructure projects.

4366
03:02:24,060 --> 03:02:27,840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: That otherwise, hindi mapapansin sa budgeting season because bottom-up budgeting to.

4367
03:02:27,860 --> 03:02:29,820
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: So this is the successor to Kalahis?

4368
03:02:29,840 --> 03:02:30,220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yes.

4369
03:02:30,460 --> 03:02:30,720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yes.

4370
03:02:30,940 --> 03:02:31,200
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Okay.

4371
03:02:31,280 --> 03:02:33,080
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Which is a successful project rin?

4372
03:02:33,100 --> 03:02:33,500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yes.

4373
03:02:34,080 --> 03:02:35,460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Sa mga information na po.

4374
03:02:35,460 --> 03:02:36,720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: We believe that it's successful.

4375
03:02:36,840 --> 03:02:43,360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Otherwise, the World Bank would not have given it or NEDA, DEPDEV would not have given it a go-signal for a successor program.

4376
03:02:43,640 --> 03:02:43,860
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Alright.

4377
03:02:46,320 --> 03:02:54,040
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: We'll take note of that kasi nakita ko na-cut yung project na nasabi na ng ating chairman to kanina.

4378
03:02:54,060 --> 03:03:00,360
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: That's why we're also evaluating yung mga cuts and also additions, actually.

4379
03:03:04,300 --> 03:03:07,900
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Actually, I don't have any more questions, Madam Chairperson.

4380
03:03:08,020 --> 03:03:08,340
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you.

4381
03:03:08,460 --> 03:03:09,140
Senator Sherwin "Win" T. Gatchalian: Thank you for that.

4382
03:03:09,700 --> 03:03:10,780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Salamat din po, SP.

4383
03:03:11,260 --> 03:03:15,540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: It looks like we will be ending earlier than expected.

4384
03:03:15,540 --> 03:03:23,940
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, pwedeng kung bigyan ng oras yung ating mga CSO representatives, resource persons.

4385
03:03:24,060 --> 03:03:32,320
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Nandito, if you'd like to take around two minutes each para i-raise yung major na mga follow-up questions nyo

4386
03:03:32,320 --> 03:03:38,280
Senator Risa Hontiveros: at yung maaring maging subject na mga proposed amendments nyo patungo sa plenary.

4387
03:03:38,520 --> 03:03:40,100
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, sino pong gustong magsalita?

4388
03:03:40,980 --> 03:03:46,540
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Ms. Gina, okay, para sa samahan ng nagkakaisang pamilya ng Pantawid.

4389
03:03:47,300 --> 03:03:48,560
Jeana Catacio: Yeah, thank you, Madam Chair.

4390
03:03:49,300 --> 03:03:52,060
Jeana Catacio: Sa lahat pong mga nandito, especially at the SWD.

4391
03:03:53,180 --> 03:03:53,980
Jeana Catacio: Siyempre po.

4392
03:03:54,060 --> 03:03:58,440
Jeana Catacio: So, ang major concern po ng samahan ng nagkakaisang pamilya ng Pantawid is the budget cut

4393
03:03:58,440 --> 03:04:01,480
Jeana Catacio: na nangyari po sa ating programa ng 4P.

4394
03:04:01,660 --> 03:04:07,440
Jeana Catacio: So, kami po ay may mga observation from 2022 up to the present.

4395
03:04:07,900 --> 03:04:11,180
Jeana Catacio: Yung mga budget cut po ay talaga nagkakaroon ng implication sa program.

4396
03:04:12,520 --> 03:04:18,360
Jeana Catacio: Of course, talaga kinakong-gratulate din naman namin si Secretary Rex dahil sa mga troubleshooting na ginawa niya

4397
03:04:18,360 --> 03:04:23,540
Jeana Catacio: at hearing those enhancements from the program ay talaga pong nagpapasalamat kami sa ano,

4398
03:04:23,540 --> 03:04:27,120
Jeana Catacio: nakikita nating direksyon ng pagpapabuti ng programa.

4399
03:04:27,580 --> 03:04:36,520
Jeana Catacio: So, balit, meron po kaming hinihiling, Madam Chair, lalong-lalong po sa version ng Senate para po sa budget ng 2027.

4400
03:04:36,820 --> 03:04:43,900
Jeana Catacio: So, nung rinisenta po ng ating butihing sekretary yung NEP 2027 doon sa House of Representatives,

4401
03:04:44,420 --> 03:04:46,240
Jeana Catacio: medyo nagkaroon po kami ng agam-agam.

4402
03:04:46,880 --> 03:04:51,640
Jeana Catacio: Dahil, siyempre, kami po ay nagkaroon ng pulong last October 7 sa PSA

4403
03:04:51,640 --> 03:04:52,220
Jeana Catacio: kung saan?

4404
03:04:52,220 --> 03:04:59,180
Jeana Catacio: Yung issue po tungkol doon sa mga nasa listahan po, ng listahan ng 3 patungo doon sa CBMS

4405
03:04:59,180 --> 03:05:01,580
Jeana Catacio: ay ito po yung klinaro namin sa PSA.

4406
03:05:02,000 --> 03:05:10,360
Jeana Catacio: Dahil marami po tayo, may mga bilang pa po tayo ng mga pantawid, supposed to be mga pantawid na hindi po napasama doon sa CBMS

4407
03:05:10,360 --> 03:05:20,080
Jeana Catacio: at sila po ay lumalapit sa samahan para po ito ay idulog po sa ating DSWD or sa ating mga mambabatas.

4408
03:05:20,080 --> 03:05:21,900
Jeana Catacio: May mga bilang po ito, Madam Chair.

4409
03:05:22,220 --> 03:05:24,980
Jeana Catacio: At sila po ay nahingian na po ng mga requirements.

4410
03:05:25,580 --> 03:05:32,080
Jeana Catacio: Dahil po ang mga mahihirap nating kababayan ang kumuha po ng tatlong birth certificate para lamang po makapasok sa programa

4411
03:05:32,080 --> 03:05:34,060
Jeana Catacio: ay napakalaki pong halaga nito.

4412
03:05:34,480 --> 03:05:39,860
Jeana Catacio: Pagkuhan ng marriage contract, pamasahe papunta po sa pagkuhan ng card, certification from school

4413
03:05:39,860 --> 03:05:47,420
Jeana Catacio: ay ito po yung ina-address namin kung bakit mahalaga po sa amin na makita yung bilang ng mga na-archive nating mga kababayan.

4414
03:05:47,420 --> 03:05:51,180
Jeana Catacio: At syempre, yung problema po ng inclusion-exclusion sa programa

4415
03:05:52,220 --> 03:06:01,040
Jeana Catacio: po ito na matugunan sapagkat marami po talaga basis sa qualified naman sila sa RA 11310 ay hindi po sila napapabilang.

4416
03:06:01,380 --> 03:06:07,480
Jeana Catacio: At meron po naman mga hindi naman na kwalifikado ay nasa programa po at nabanggit ito ni Secretary kanina.

4417
03:06:07,980 --> 03:06:13,900
Jeana Catacio: So ito po yung aming mga inilabi sa iba't ibang ahensya na makakatulong po sa ating mga kababayang mahirap.

4418
03:06:13,900 --> 03:06:22,040
Jeana Catacio: Tama po kanina si SB no po at nakakatuwa po na merami pong graduate na mga pantawid.

4419
03:06:22,220 --> 03:06:23,720
Jeana Catacio: So ito po yung mga mga household mula po sa programa.

4420
03:06:24,140 --> 03:06:31,740
Jeana Catacio: Subalit hindi po ito tumutukoy doon sa mga mga mga kababayan pa natin na mahihirap dahil galing na rin po sa PSA.

4421
03:06:32,180 --> 03:06:43,760
Jeana Catacio: Meron pa po tayong mga kababayan na 3.2 million na mga mahihirap at meron po tayong mga waiting list na mga mahihirap din na supposed to be ay mapabilang po sa programa o makapaloob sa programa.

4422
03:06:43,960 --> 03:06:51,520
Jeana Catacio: Kung nakikita po natin na ang four-piece program po ay isang instrumento na talaga pong nakakapag-alleviate sa ating mga kababayan.

4423
03:06:52,220 --> 03:07:00,240
Jeana Catacio: So doon sa pag-aaral ng World Bank, 2.2 million household po ay nakapagpaangat sa ating mga kababayan mula sa kahirapan.

4424
03:07:00,240 --> 03:07:18,740
Jeana Catacio: Nawa po ay marinig po ng ating mga senador, madam chair, senate president, ang aming pong pagdulog na panatilihin ang budget para po doon sa pagpapanatili ng 4.4 million na mga household na makapasok po sa ating pantawid program.

4425
03:07:19,100 --> 03:07:21,740
Jeana Catacio: Sapagkat mahalaga po sa amin ang bilang.

4426
03:07:22,220 --> 03:07:30,780
Jeana Catacio: Kukunti man ito pero ang tinitignan po natin ay yung mga kabataan na talaga pong ma-address yung kanilang pag-aaral.

4427
03:07:30,860 --> 03:07:42,880
Jeana Catacio: At salamat sekretary, nakita namin doon sa inyo pong mga nabanggit kanina na yung tertiary education po ay talagang ito po yung major concern ng ating mga exiting mga pantawid beneficiary.

4428
03:07:42,880 --> 03:07:49,880
Jeana Catacio: At sa paunti-unti po sana sa direction ng ating four-piece program sa mga susunod pong taon ay ito po talaga yung matugunan.

4429
03:07:49,880 --> 03:07:56,460
Jeana Catacio: So marami po kami mga idinulog na mga recommendation tungkol po sa tertiary education at livelihood.

4430
03:07:57,140 --> 03:08:10,800
Jeana Catacio: Ito po sana, itong mga convergence na tulong ng ating mga ahensya, nawa po pag-materialize po ito sa mga susunod na taon para po hindi na po talaga bumalik sa kahirapan yung mga nag-exit na ating mga kababayan.

4431
03:08:10,800 --> 03:08:17,560
Jeana Catacio: So tama po, makagraduate lamang po ang isa sa ating mga monitored child sa program at makapag-kolehyo.

4432
03:08:17,980 --> 03:08:19,800
Jeana Catacio: Malaking tulong po yan sa mga pamilya.

4433
03:08:19,880 --> 03:08:23,880
Jeana Catacio: Sa kanila pong pamilya para po tuluyan po silang makagraduate sa pantawid.

4434
03:08:24,540 --> 03:08:39,340
Jeana Catacio: At ito naman po ang ating dream para po sa mga susunod pong taon na marami pa pong four-piece na makagraduate na talaga pong nakuha natin yung objective ng program na sila po ay hindi na magpa-backslide at nakatawid po talaga sa kahirapan.

4435
03:08:39,720 --> 03:08:41,620
Jeana Catacio: Maraming salamat sa opportunity, Madam Chair.

4436
03:08:42,000 --> 03:08:43,740
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Maraming salamat din po, Ms. Gina.

4437
03:08:44,120 --> 03:08:47,980
Senator Risa Hontiveros: Secrex, gusto nyo bang pagunan initially yung mga idinulog na sa...

4438
03:08:47,980 --> 03:08:49,840
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Madam Chair, si Jenna lagi yan sa office ko.

4439
03:08:49,880 --> 03:08:50,460
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Suki yan.

4440
03:08:51,320 --> 03:08:52,080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And her group.

4441
03:08:52,180 --> 03:08:56,100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: And they're very helpful in trying to tell me kung ano ho yung nangyayari sa ground.

4442
03:08:56,760 --> 03:09:06,160
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ang gusto ko lang ho una i-assure ang mga nakikinig na mga four-piece na yung pagbawa sa budget this year, hindi ho siya tulad, magiging epekto tulad noon na naghabol tayo.

4443
03:09:06,160 --> 03:09:17,720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kung matatandaan nyo, di ba meron tayong pagtitipo na nung, I forgot that was 2025, na yung budget cut was severe, nag-worry talaga sila.

4444
03:09:17,860 --> 03:09:19,720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero ang gusto ko lang i-report naman na...

4445
03:09:19,880 --> 03:09:20,600
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Nahabol ho yun.

4446
03:09:20,700 --> 03:09:22,660
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Binigyan kami ng augmentation na ibalik yun.

4447
03:09:23,080 --> 03:09:25,820
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero syempre yung pangamba, yun yung iniiwasan natin.

4448
03:09:26,240 --> 03:09:33,360
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: This year, yung budget cut ho, hindi naman ho [unclear] out of no rational.

4449
03:09:33,720 --> 03:09:41,140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kundi dahil lumiit na ho yung catchment natin to 3.5 million households or families, ma-excess na ho siya.

4450
03:09:41,580 --> 03:09:44,440
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So hindi ho naman ho makakompromise yung programa.

4451
03:09:44,740 --> 03:09:45,860
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yun ang ina-assure ko sa kanila.

4452
03:09:46,280 --> 03:09:49,720
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Alam ko saan ang gagaling si Jenna dahil yung original na mga cut nangamba talaga sila.

4453
03:09:49,720 --> 03:09:53,540
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: But yung cut ngayon is brought about by data na 3.5 na lang kami.

4454
03:09:53,680 --> 03:09:55,320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So talagang niliitan.

4455
03:09:55,740 --> 03:10:02,140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero tulad rin ang napaliwanag ko kanina, hindi naman magkakaroon ng decline sa quality ng programa.

4456
03:10:02,280 --> 03:10:04,100
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Bagamat marami pang enhancements.

4457
03:10:04,220 --> 03:10:07,940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Katulad nga yung ilo-launch natin ngayon this year na ESSI.

4458
03:10:08,600 --> 03:10:10,740
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Alam nila yung ESSI, yun yung kune-kwento ko kanina.

4459
03:10:10,900 --> 03:10:13,280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Dati yung ESSI kasi marami ho siyang laman.

4460
03:10:13,800 --> 03:10:16,280
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Pero ngayon, we just focused on the monitored children.

4461
03:10:16,820 --> 03:10:18,220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So this December, we're launching it.

4462
03:10:18,220 --> 03:10:18,900
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yun yung kune-kwento ko.

4463
03:10:19,000 --> 03:10:19,240
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Tuloy.

4464
03:10:19,720 --> 03:10:22,920
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Tuloy kolehyo, tuloy aral, tuloy trabaho.

4465
03:10:22,920 --> 03:10:30,480
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Whether tech voc man yan or academic man yan, tutulungan natin yung kanila mga monitored children.

4466
03:10:31,480 --> 03:10:36,340
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Yun ho ang assurance ko sa ating mga civil society, sa ating group na SNP.

4467
03:10:38,480 --> 03:10:41,580
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Huwag kayong mag-worry na yung budget cut this time hindi arbitrary.

4468
03:10:42,140 --> 03:10:45,500
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Kung hindi, this is driven by the data na lumiit ho tayo.

4469
03:10:46,000 --> 03:10:47,620
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Walang magsasuffer sa services.

4470
03:10:48,500 --> 03:10:48,940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: In fact,

4471
03:10:48,940 --> 03:10:51,080
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: na-regularize pa yung mga links natin.

4472
03:10:51,640 --> 03:10:53,140
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Tapos, makailan lang, kahapon lang,

4473
03:10:53,300 --> 03:10:58,320
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: binigyan kami ng balita ng ating BBM na dadagdag pa yung mga SWA o Social Welfare Assistant.

4474
03:10:58,920 --> 03:11:00,940
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: So, from a ratio of 500, no?

4475
03:11:01,100 --> 03:11:01,780
Senator Risa Hontiveros: 1,000.

4476
03:11:01,780 --> 03:11:02,900
Senator Risa Hontiveros: So, naging 1 is to 500.

4477
03:11:03,100 --> 03:11:06,800
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: Ngayon kasi yung Social Welfare Assistant, from 1 is to 1,000 families,

4478
03:11:06,940 --> 03:11:09,220
DSWD Secretary Rex Gatchalian: ngayon magiging 1 is to 500 na lang.

